{
  "transcriptVersion": 1,
  "id": "keyring-recovery",
  "description": "The recovery blob (WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §13.11.2). A ring made without one answers the fetch 404 not_found. The device that holds the root sets a sealed 61-byte blob (204; the epoch and kid are the ring's), and a fetch returns it: 200 with ct, only to a signed-in device of the account. A device may fetch 5 times a day, counting the 404: the sixth is 429 rate_limited with Retry-After. Each fetch is audited and emailed to the account. The blob is an opaque fixture: the server never sees the code that seals it.",
  "features": ["sync.keyring"],
  "requires": ["core.store"],
  "product": "djdl",
  "baseUrl": "https://key.plrs.im",
  "now": 1700000000,
  "trust": {
    "pkey-test-prod-2026": "kDJF6Deuexo91hFZ9TAPr2SmjUEuTXdia67UogTEpkI"
  },
  "initial": {
    "deviceId": "TRANSCRIPTDEVICE0000000000000001",
    "token": "pkeyt_S22Hra5u0qN7HPluRUE5KOWim5z4-yZ1OdJIwjDRou0",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "steps": [
